{
  "format": "dive-source-occupancy-v1",
  "source": {
    "corpus": "tlaplus/Examples 6a7b26a31c1a6aeec789b455e9bbfa3b3ad2728f, specifications/transaction_commit",
    "module": "Original TCommit.tla. Only enlarge RM to {r1, r2, \u2026, rN} in TCommit.cfg. Keep TCSpec, TCTypeOK, TCConsistent and CHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE. No configured symmetry.",
    "second_source": "Crew is the cyclic fixture actually read by scripts/symbolic/check_occupancy.py. Set CrewIds to the same model-value domain, Chief=r1, INIT StartState, NEXT Step, INVARIANTS Bounds Safe and CHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE. Chief is unused on the positive path.",
    "negative_edits": "For NonePrepared extend TCommit with the invariant that every manager status differs from \"prepared\", and append INVARIANT NonePrepared. For the 8192-manager initial control, extend TCommit with NoneWorking (every status differs from \"working\") and select INVARIANTS NoneWorking TCTypeOK TCConsistent. Original actions and properties remain selected in all TCommit tests.",
    "module_sha256": {
      "TCommit.tla": "98974d8c5ee007f4f62188737c20c7dcdb05af099cc53a59c8b8651331fd925d",
      "Crew.tla": "b774e97ff6b654f1ebf5d910f1c49863a1e1b36ee0ba075c1737111314d4885d",
      "Prepared.tla": "4689584fd7546e5c92bbe5fdf9d141c5ade9ab285b39c9d7a95a6222df2c77c7",
      "Working.tla": "6ba42a68523bb3761af3d8cf5507bff2d68fc754d38ffb1294d0e91a806bcae6"
    },
    "negative_configs_sha256": {
      "NonePrepared-1000": "e5b5f872abc128601361af2518efc4693b875532285cf114b47d8c6bae8c08c9",
      "NonePrepared-2048": "a3623c2898200d33257317e1e0fee69dbf9cfdd3af149657d74fd9365ec06045",
      "NonePrepared-4096": "793bd4792a3618977e5b50820cbf1fdaf35b52b0aa0511a75b5082830e0888fd",
      "NoneWorking-8192": "68316cc3ac3f26e4c3dbd0017e5c8187a6222da18e5e945e1935c113e0578b08"
    }
  },
  "method": "EC2 c7i.4xlarge, 16 vCPUs on 8 Intel Xeon Platinum 8488C physical cores, Ubuntu 24.04.5. New installed CLI processes, pinned to separate physical cores while other campaigns ran. GNU time includes startup, frontend, quotient search and any required independent replay. RSS is peak KiB, timings are samples. All success counts in cases are actual full BFS output. Each was matched to independent exact formulas for distinct, generated, depth and occupancy count.",
  "meaning": "The graph traversed by BFS is the exact permutation quotient proven from the one-table source grammar. Count each orbit by its exact multinomial weight for ordinary labeled output. Count each enabled original owner witness and every duplicate/stutter. Depth is one-step BFS depth, including Init. Relations, guards and properties are compiled from bound IR without a TCommit or Crew formula in the worker.",
  "commands": [
    "python3 scripts/symbolic/check_occupancy.py PATH/transaction_commit --dive DIVE --installed",
    "dive check TCommit.tla --config R8192.cfg --strategy occupancy --type-invariant TCTypeOK --max-orbits 34500000 --time-limit 380s --max-memory 3900m --output json",
    "dive check Prepared.tla --config Bad4096.cfg --strategy occupancy --type-invariant TCTypeOK --time-limit 620s --max-memory 1800m --trace word.json --output json",
    "dive validate-trace Prepared.tla --config Bad4096.cfg --trace word.json --compat=tlc --output json",
    "dive check Crew.tla --config Crew4096.cfg --strategy occupancy --type-invariant Bounds --max-orbits 1000000 --time-limit 375s --max-memory 3900m --output json"
  ],
  "oracles": {
    "TCommit": "Weighted distinct=3^n+2^n\u22121; generated=1+n(3^n+2^(n\u22121)); depth=2n+1; occupancies=binomial(n+2,2)+n. Before any commit each manager may be working, prepared or aborted. After a commit each is prepared or committed. The all-prepared vector overlaps.",
    "Crew": "A=2^n assignments with no busy owner; B=n\u00b72^(n\u22121) assignments with one busy owner. I=B+n(n\u22121)\u00b72^(n\u22122) is the total idle count over both regions. Distinct=A+B. Generated=2+2I+2B+(n+1)(A+B): two Init witnesses, two Wait branches per idle owner, Begin and End, n owner stutters plus one global stutter. Depth=n+2 and occupancies=2n+1 for n>=1. Neither formula is used by the checker."
  },
